  partName: Cylinder Head Bolt (2)
  description: The Cylinder Head Bolt (2) is another instance of the tiny, complex-shaped
    bolt, also positioned at the top-center-center of the engine, fabricated from
    Material.001. Its primary function is to provide additional clamping force to
    the cylinder head, supplementing the sealing process and contributing to the
    engine's overall efficiency. Notably, the multiple bolts work in tandem to maintain
    a consistent, high-pressure environment within the engine.
